# Acceptance test: known-good encodings (ASHRAE 135 clause 20.2 examples) and round trips.
# Blocks real-nan-encoded .. encoder-capacity are CR-102 regression vectors: edge cases (NaN/Inf,
# length and tag-number boundaries, capacity limits) whose output had to stay exactly as before the
# CR-102 refactor. CR-103 item 2 deliberately changed the two NaN blocks: NaN used to be rejected
# (ERR) and is now encoded like any other bit pattern.
# Blocks from char-string-utf8-valid onwards are CR-103 vectors (UTF-8 validation, NaN, and
# Unsigned/Enumerated 0 keeping its one content octet).
